From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rust-mos-sync <rust-mos-sync@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bootstrap: vendor a patched `cc` recognizing the MOS
 architecture

Bootstrap unconditionally probes a C compiler for every configured
target (utils/cc_detect.rs: "for building shims ... and being a linker
for Rust code"), even a pure no_std target with no C code at all. That
probe goes through the `cc` crate, which parses the target triple and
rejects any architecture it does not know - "mos" isn't one of them,
upstream (checked against rust-lang/cc-rs main, 2026-09-27: still
absent, no open issue or PR either).

Vendor cc 1.2.28 (the version this rustc pins) with one added match
arm, alongside avr/msp430/m68k, and patch it in via
`[patch.crates-io]` in src/bootstrap/Cargo.toml. To be dropped once
upstream adds MOS support; see rust-mos-sync docs/backlog.md.
